  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "The prosed works include the following;\n1. Replacement of existing fire damaged hipped roof with gabled roof.\n2. Proposed loft conversion including dormer extension to rear of property.\n3. Proposed single story extension to rear of property.\n4. Various internal alterations including the provision of en-suite bathrooms to all of the existing bedrooms.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single storey rear extension, together with the proposed hip to gable roof extension, due to its excessive size and scale, and inappropriate position and design, would fail to respect the proportions of the original house and would disrupt the symmetry of the short run of terraced houses, harmful to the overall character and appearance of the site and surrounding area, contrary to the Residential Extensions Guidelines SPD and Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations).",
    "Reason : 2 - As a result of the excessive depth of the rear extension, the single storey rear extension would harm the living conditions of the adjoining neighbour no. 171 Ellerdine Road through an increased sense of enclosure and undue loss of outlook. The proposal therefore fails to comply with adopted Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations) and the Residential Extension Guidelines as set out within the adopted Character Sustainability and Design Codes SPD."
  ],
